        <property name="text">
         <string>&lt;html&gt;&lt;head/&gt;&lt;body&gt;&lt;p&gt;openEarthCAD is provided to the general public under an open-source license. openEarthCAD also makes use of other open-source software. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;These may be licensed under different, but compatible, open-source licenses.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;openEarthCAD uses the open-source Qt toolkit, version 6, and is primarily written in Python 3.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Many graphics/images were used from &lt;a href=&quot;https://openclipart.org/&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; text-decoration: underline; color:#2980b9;&quot;&gt;openclipart.org&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. These images are either under the public domain or the&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; text-decoration: underline; color:#2980b9;&quot;&gt;Creative Commons Zero 1.0 Public Domain License&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. All other images are released to the public domain, with the exception of the Libranext &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;quot;L&amp;quot; logo and its variations.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;While we don't restrict these use cases through licensing, &lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;we strongly condemn&lt;/span&gt; the unethical use of this software, such as in military &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;applications, warfare, or nuclear weapons. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</string>
        </property>
       </widget>
